    "long_instructions": "Your community now wants to test your program to make a prediction for the upcoming week. \r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Add one of the following lines to the top of your program to import a dictionary of features to make a prediction about:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom next_week import pantry\r\nfrom next_week import road\r\nfrom next_week import polling_place\r\nfrom next_week import tree\r\n```\r\n2. Convert the dictionary into a list of numerical features. Be sure to use the same order of features that you used when defining inputs to your neural network!\r\n3. Use your model to make a prediction about the data for next week.\r\n4. Print a specific decision to make based on the prediction.\r\n5. Experiment with changing the feature values in `next_week.py` and re-running your code. How does your decision change based on the data?\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRecall that if `model` is a model and `x` is a list of numerical features, then `model.predict([x])[0]` will use your model to generate a prediction for `x`.\r\n\r\nAsk AI Tutor for help if you get stuck!\r\n",
